  "conclusion": "False alarms: 0 of 6 undrifted months flagged (highest PSI 0.02985 against a 0.25 threshold), so the detector is not simply flagging everything. feature_shift_recency_x1.8: flagged after 0 scoring month(s) with max PSI 0.32195, PR-AUC 0.8412 -> 0.7148, label-visible drop after 0 month(s) of matured labels, retraining triggers ['RT-1', 'RT-2', 'RT-3', 'RT-5', 'RT-6']. segment_shift_one_country: flagged after 0 scoring month(s) with max PSI 1.13428, PR-AUC 0.8412 -> 0.7534, label-visible drop after 0 month(s) of matured labels, retraining triggers ['RT-1', 'RT-2', 'RT-3', 'RT-5', 'RT-6']. The PRD's expected observation is confirmed in the gap between the two delays: feature drift is visible from the scoring data alone, with no labels at all, while the performance drop only becomes measurable once labels have matured - which in production is 90 days later. Status is partial because the approval half of the hypothesis is covered elsewhere, not here.",
  "limitations": [
    "The approval half of the hypothesis - that the challenger is compared with the champion and promotion waits for approval - is not re-tested here. It is the approval gate of the main pipeline, covered by AT-08/AT-13 and demonstrated by scripts/run_demo.py; repeating it inside a drift experiment would measure the gate twice and the drift detectors once.",
    "Replay is over synthetic months, not Online Retail II. Only the generator can be told to shift one feature or change one segment's behaviour on demand, which is what the independent variable requires."
  ],
